36	// New-chain answer (range 1..4):  8 occurrences over 4 blocks, tip 4.
37	//
38	// The suffix transaction sets are disjoint ({a,c,d,e,f,g} vs {p,q,r,s}) and
39	// every suffix hash differs, so the two complete answers are observably
40	// different not just in their counts but in every record above height 2. A
41	// page that happens to stay ordered (e.g. one new-chain hit followed by one
42	// old-chain hit at consecutive positions) is still a torn answer and must be
